  "review_notes": [
    "Gate 8 is the first full-size feedback iteration after the 100 mm print and remains a review/prototype candidate.",
    "The central diffuser is narrowed by two opaque structural muzzle rails, which tie the weak nose halves into the lower and upper opaque shells while blocking eye-to-center light spill.",
    "Every main flange module is larger and uses two M3 fasteners. Each ear has one broad four-fastener saddle plus continuous seam rails.",
    "Internal triangular panel ribs are enlarged, and continuous rectangular rails now reinforce both sides of inter-shell opaque seams.",
    "The rear base is a shallow 5 mm outward frame secured by six rear-loaded M5 bolts to 28 x 36 x 10 mm structural pads; the two horizontal centers are X +/-15 mm and each pad provides a 14 mm nut/tool envelope.",
    "Two blind 20.50 mm sockets are integral with the upper-head shell STLs for nominal 19.05 mm Everbilt 6605 aluminum square tubing. One transverse M4 bolt passes through each printed socket and the drilled aluminum tube; there are no exterior shell holes or separate clamp caps.",
    "Print the one-piece portal fit coupon and one representative flange/seam coupon before committing to full shell prints."
  ]
